/-!
# `row_residue` for q = 2 through `ZMod 11`

`vSeedPrime 2 = 11`.  Data (all checked exactly in Python, see `checks/`):
* `q2rzD r` is the lcm of the denominators of row `r` of
  `q2SourceMatrixAtZeroExplicit`; `q2rzN0 = diag(q2rzD) * M_0` and
  `q2rzAN = diag(q2rzD) * A` are integer matrices, so
  `diag(q2rzD) * M_t = q2rzN0 - t * q2rzAN`;
* for `t = 0..4`, `q2rzE * q2rzNbar_t = q2rzL_t * q2rzU_t` in `ZMod 11`, with
  `q2rzE` upper and `q2rzL_t` lower unitriangular, and `q2rzNbar_t` the residue of
  `q2rzN0 - t * q2rzAN`;
* `q2rzW` inverts the Vandermonde matrix `(tʲ)` modulo 11.

No rational determinant at `T ≠ 0`, no rational interpolation, and no 9 by 9
Leibniz expansion occurs.  Every `decide` acts on entries below 11, on one
`ℤ → ZMod 11` cast, on one 9-term dot product, or on the product of nine
small naturals.  Determinants are reached only through `Matrix.det_mul`,
`Matrix.det_of_isUpperTriangular`/`isLowerTriangular` and `RingHom.map_det`.
Exact coefficient residues: [4, 2, 7, 3, 9] = `vSeedResidueRow 2`.
-/

namespace Li2Lean.B3

noncomputable section

open Li2Lean
open Matrix

set_option maxRecDepth 1000000
set_option maxHeartbeats 20000000

instance q2rzFact : Fact (Nat.Prime (vSeedPrime 2)) := ⟨by norm_num [vSeedPrime]⟩

